<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alessandro Sforza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1409">1409</a>–<a href="/years/1473">1473</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-sforza">House of Sforza</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alessandro Sforza was a condottiero and the younger brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesco-sforza">Francesco Sforza</a>, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>. In 1445 he bought Pesaro from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galeazzo-malatesta">Galeazzo Malatesta</a>, whose granddaughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/costanza-da-varano">Costanza da Varano</a> he had married, and he ruled it as papal vicar until his death. He made Pesaro a cultivated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> court, and his descendants held the lordship until 1512.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alessandro-sforza.jpg" alt="Alessandro Sforza" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sailko · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rogier_van_der_weyden_(bottega),_trittico_sforza,_07.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1445 Galeazzo Malatesta sold Pesaro to <b>Alessandro Sforza</b>, brother of Francesco Sforza, who had married his granddaughter Costanza da Varano.</blockquote><a href="/state/lordship-of-pesaro">Lordship of Pesaro</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Cotignola, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. Died in Pesaro, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=44.38,11.93&amp;year=1450" aria-label="Cotignola on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4835 594 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Alessandro Sforza"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5285 864h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5285 864h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=44.38,11.93&amp;year=1450">What was here in 1450? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
